# zstd -- the compressor libarchive and flatpak both want.
#
# Needed by libarchive (which flatpak takes as a hard dependency for OCI layers
# and .flatpak bundles) and by flatpak's own -Dlibzstd option for delta
# transport. The kernel already has zstd built in for squashfs; this is the
# userspace library and CLI.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/facebook/zstd/releases/download/v1.5.7/zstd-1.5.7.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=eb33e51f49a15e023950cd7825ca74a4a2b43db8354825ac24fc1b7ee09e6fa3
SRC_DIR=zstd-1.5.7

# NO CONFIGURE_ARGS AND NO MESON_ARGS BECAUSE THERE IS NO CONFIGURE AND NO
# MESON. zstd ships a plain Makefile, so this recipe carries its own build.sh
# and install.sh. It is the first package here that cannot use a shared stage.
#
# THE VARIABLES BELOW ARE THE WHOLE REASON THIS RECIPE NEEDS COMMENTS.
# programs/Makefile does not offer options -- it PROBES, by compiling a test
# program and setting a variable from whether the compile succeeded:
#
#     HAVE_ZLIB ?= $(shell printf '#include <zlib.h>\nint main(void){return 0;}' > have_zlib.c \
#                  && $(CC) $(FLAGS) -o have_zlib have_zlib.c -lz 2> /dev/null && echo 1 || echo 0; ...)
#
# and the same for HAVE_LZMA and HAVE_LZ4. zlib and xz ARE packaged here, so
# left alone the probe would succeed for both and the zstd CLI would link -lz
# and -llzma to gain --format=gzip and --format=xz.
#
# THAT IS WORSE THAN A FEATURE ARRIVING UNASKED: IT WOULD GIVE THIS PACKAGE TWO
# RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES THAT THE RECIPE DOES NOT DECLARE, decided by what happened
# to be in the builder image rather than by anything written down. tape's
# dependency graph would be wrong, silently, and only for the CLI -- libzstd
# itself is unaffected either way.
#
# So all three are pinned to 0. Nothing in the flatpak chain wants zstd's gzip
# or xz passthrough: libarchive and flatpak use libzstd, and gzip and xz already
# have their own tools here. LZ4 is not packaged, so its probe would answer 0
# anyway -- it is named regardless, because "answers 0 today because the library
# is missing" and "answers 0 because we chose that" are different facts, and only
# one of them survives lz4 being packaged later.
ZSTD_MAKE_VARS="HAVE_ZLIB=0 HAVE_LZMA=0 HAVE_LZ4=0"
